# Hardware sketches and host regression tests

This directory contains individual hardware/bring-up sketches (AS5600, encoder,
IMU, I2C, motor and Wi-Fi). They are not the host regression suite and may need
hardware-specific setup. Motor sketches can move the real robot. Read
../../docs/safety.md and inspect the sketch before flashing or running one.
Do not assume `pio test` runs the project's complete regression suite.

Run the maintained C++ host suites from the repository root:

    docker\mor_luam.bat fw-test

This compiles ../test_host/tests.cpp and ../test_host/nav_runner_tests.cpp in
Docker. It does not connect to or move a robot. Ubuntu uses
./docker/mor_luam.sh fw-test.

Browser/mock checks from the repository root (Node.js / Python on the PC):

    node firmware/web/test_simulation.cjs
    node firmware/web/test_simulation_noise.cjs
    node firmware/web/test_route_test.cjs
    python firmware/web/test_mock_route_test.py
    python tools/imu_shake.py --self-test

Real-robot acceptance tests are in ../../tools/robot_test.py; steps 2-4 MOVE the
robot and require the owner beside it. Commands and evidence: ../../docs/testing.md
